      "cml:premiseText": "You need to be willing to make a pledge of commitment.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "You can apply for citizenship by conferral."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-3-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "3 Definitions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-3-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf, p.11",
      "values:originalText": "In this Act:\nadverse security assessment has the meaning given by section 35\nof the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act 1979.\nartificial conception procedure includes:\n\n(a) artificial insemination; and\n\n(b) the implantation of an embryo in the body of a woman.\nAustralia, when used in a geographical sense, includes the external\nTerritories.\nAustralian citizen has the meaning given by section 4.\nAustralian law means a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a\nTerritory.\nbogus document has the same meaning as in subsection 5(1) of the\nMigration Act 1958.\nchild: without limiting who is a child of a person for the purposes\nof this Act, each of the following is the child of a person:\n\n(a) an adopted child, stepchild or exnuptial child of the person;\n\n(b) someone who is a child of the person within the meaning of\nthe Family Law Act 1975.\ncitizenship law means:\n\n(a) this Act; and\n\n(b) the regulations; and\n\n(c) any legislative instrument made under this Act or the\nregulations.\ncommencement day means the day on which sections 2A to 54 (as\noriginally enacted) commence.\nde facto partner has the meaning given by the Acts Interpretation\nAct 1901.",
      "skos:definition": "In this Act:\nadverse security assessment has the meaning given by section 35\nof the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act 1979.\nartificial conception procedure includes:\n\n(a) artificial insemination; and\n\n(b) the implantation of an embryo in the body of a woman.\nAustralia, when used in a geographical sense, includes the external\nTerritories.\nAustralian citizen has the meaning given by section 4.\nAustralian law means a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a\nTerritory.\nbogus document has the same meaning as in subsection 5(1) of the\nMigration Act 1958.\nchild: without limiting who is a child of a person for the purposes\nof this Act, each of the following is the child of a person:\n\n(a) an adopted child, stepchild or exnuptial child of the person;\n\n(b) someone who is a child of the person within the meaning of\nthe Family Law Act 1975.\ncitizenship law means:\n\n(a) this Act; and\n\n(b) the regulations; and\n\n(c) any legislative instrument made under this Act or the\nregulations.\ncommencement day means the day on which sections 2A to 54 (as\noriginally enacted) commence.\nde facto partner has the meaning given by the Acts Interpretation\nAct 1901.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-3-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-3-2-logic-descriptionlogic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-3-2-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "44eb8983e3fb55f5aafc575f7df4bc32a9afb5345fde9c13251fdd40aae5ded8",
      "skos:note": "Defines terms used in the Act"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-3-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "3 Definitions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 11,
      "values:originalText": "In this Act:\nadverse security assessment has the meaning given by section 35\nof the Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act 1979.\nartificial conception procedure includes:\n\n(a) artificial insemination; and\n\n(b) the implantation of an embryo in the body of a woman.\nAustralia, when used in a geographical sense, includes the external\nTerritories.\nAustralian citizen has the meaning given by section 4.\nAustralian law means a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a\nTerritory.\nbogus document has the same meaning as in subsection 5(1) of the\nMigration Act 1958.\nchild: without limiting who is a child of a person for the purposes\nof this Act, each of the following is the child of a person:\n\n(a) an adopted child, stepchild or exnuptial child of the person;\n\n(b) someone who is a child of the person within the meaning of\nthe Family Law Act 1975.\ncitizenship law means:\n\n(a) this Act; and\n\n(b) the regulations; and\n\n(c) any legislative instrument made under this Act or the\nregulations.\ncommencement day means the day on which sections 2A to 54 (as\noriginally enacted) commence.\nde facto partner has the meaning given by the Acts Interpretation\nAct 1901."
    },
