      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf, p.13",
      "values:originalText": "(b) in relation to any time before 4 June 1969—includes a\nreference to the Island of Nauru.\nold Act means the Australian Citizenship Act 1948 as in force at\nany time before the commencement day.\nordinarily resident: a person is taken to be ordinarily resident in a\ncountry if and only if:\n\n(a) he or she has his or her home in that country; or\n\n(b) that country is the country of his or her permanent abode\neven if he or she is temporarily absent from that country.",
      "skos:definition": "(b) in relation to any time before 4 June 1969—includes a\nreference to the Island of Nauru.\nold Act means the Australian Citizenship Act 1948 as in force at\nany time before the commencement day.\nordinarily resident: a person is taken to be ordinarily resident in a\ncountry if and only if:\n\n(a) he or she has his or her home in that country; or\n\n(b) that country is the country of his or her permanent abode\neven if he or she is temporarily absent from that country.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-16-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "88c6eb53be277a642ae5ced08e2c53f892099f0eb6b42e9aceede362bb956449",
      "skos:note": "Definition of ordinarily resident in a country"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-16",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "16 September 1975; and",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 13,
      "values:originalText": "(b) in relation to any time before 4 June 1969—includes a\nreference to the Island of Nauru.\nold Act means the Australian Citizenship Act 1948 as in force at\nany time before the commencement day.\nordinarily resident: a person is taken to be ordinarily resident in a\ncountry if and only if:\n\n(a) he or she has his or her home in that country; or\n\n(b) that country is the country of his or her permanent abode\neven if he or she is temporarily absent from that country."
    },
