        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-4-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3f960f21519b3e8614a1d9be4f3c14914c9906f5b695acb6e2006d66d6ed21ed"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 Australian citizen",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 15,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, Australian citizen means a person\nwho:\n\n(a) is an Australian citizen under Division 1 or 2 of Part 2; or\n\n(b) satisfies both of the following:\n\n(i) the person was an Australian citizen under the\nAustralian Citizenship Act 1948 immediately before the\ncommencement day;\n\n(ii) the person has not ceased to be an Australian citizen\nunder this Act.\nCitizenship under the old Act\n\n(2) If, under this Act, it is necessary to work out if a person was an\nAustralian citizen at a time before the commencement day, work\nthat out under the Australian Citizenship Act 1948 as in force at\nthat time."
    },
