    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6 Responsible parent",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf, p.16",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, a person is a responsible parent in\nrelation to a child if and only if:\n\n\nPreliminary  Part 1\n\nSection 6A\n\nAustralian Citizenship Act 2007\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) the person is a parent of the child except where, because of\norders made under the Family Law Act 1975, the person no\nlonger has any parental responsibility for the child; or\n\n(b) under a parenting order the child is to live with the person\n(whether or not the person is a parent of the child); or\n\n(c) under a parenting order the person has parental responsibility\nfor the child’s long-term or day-to-day care, welfare and\ndevelopment (whether or not the person is a parent of the\nchild); or\n\n(d) the person (whether or not a parent of the child) has\nguardianship or custody of the child, jointly or otherwise,\nunder an Australian law or a foreign law, whether because of\nadoption, operation of law, an order of a court or otherwise.\n\n(1A) In paragraph (1)(a):\nparental responsibility has the same meaning as in Part VII of the\nFamily Law Act 1975.\n\n(2) Expressions used in paragraphs (1)(b) and (c) have the same\nmeaning as in the Family Law Act 1975.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, a person is a responsible parent in\nrelation to a child if and only if:\n\n\nPreliminary  Part 1\n\nSection 6A\n\nAustralian Citizenship Act 2007\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) the person is a parent of the child except where, because of\norders made under the Family Law Act 1975, the person no\nlonger has any parental responsibility for the child; or\n\n(b) under a parenting order the child is to live with the person\n(whether or not the person is a parent of the child); or\n\n(c) under a parenting order the person has parental responsibility\nfor the child’s long-term or day-to-day care, welfare and\ndevelopment (whether or not the person is a parent of the\nchild); or\n\n(d) the person (whether or not a parent of the child) has\nguardianship or custody of the child, jointly or otherwise,\nunder an Australian law or a foreign law, whether because of\nadoption, operation of law, an order of a court or otherwise.\n\n(1A) In paragraph (1)(a):\nparental responsibility has the same meaning as in Part VII of the\nFamily Law Act 1975.\n\n(2) Expressions used in paragraphs (1)(b) and (c) have the same\nmeaning as in the Family Law Act 1975.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-6-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-6-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-6-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "13a445df539e990b9dff16fd5c1196274105bf50079c23be6035cb5a0b329010"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6 Responsible parent",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 16,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, a person is a responsible parent in\nrelation to a child if and only if:\n\n\nPreliminary  Part 1\n\nSection 6A\n\nAustralian Citizenship Act 2007\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) the person is a parent of the child except where, because of\norders made under the Family Law Act 1975, the person no\nlonger has any parental responsibility for the child; or\n\n(b) under a parenting order the child is to live with the person\n(whether or not the person is a parent of the child); or\n\n(c) under a parenting order the person has parental responsibility\nfor the child’s long-term or day-to-day care, welfare and\ndevelopment (whether or not the person is a parent of the\nchild); or\n\n(d) the person (whether or not a parent of the child) has\nguardianship or custody of the child, jointly or otherwise,\nunder an Australian law or a foreign law, whether because of\nadoption, operation of law, an order of a court or otherwise.\n\n(1A) In paragraph (1)(a):\nparental responsibility has the same meaning as in Part VII of the\nFamily Law Act 1975.\n\n(2) Expressions used in paragraphs (1)(b) and (c) have the same\nmeaning as in the Family Law Act 1975."
    },
