    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-7",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "7 Children born on ships or aircraft or after death of parent",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-7"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf, p.18",
      "values:originalText": "Persons born on ships or aircraft\n\n(1) For the purposes of this Act:\n\n(a) a person born on a ship or aircraft registered in Australia or a\nforeign country is taken to have been born at the place at\nwhich the ship or aircraft is registered; and\n\n(b) a person born on a ship or aircraft not registered in Australia\nor a foreign country and belonging to the government of a\ncountry is taken to have been born in that country.\nPersons born after death of parent\n\n(2) For the purposes of this Act, the status of a parent of a person at the\ntime of the person’s birth is, for a parent who died before the birth,\ntaken to be the status of the parent when the parent died.",
      "skos:definition": "Persons born on ships or aircraft\n\n(1) For the purposes of this Act:\n\n(a) a person born on a ship or aircraft registered in Australia or a\nforeign country is taken to have been born at the place at\nwhich the ship or aircraft is registered; and\n\n(b) a person born on a ship or aircraft not registered in Australia\nor a foreign country and belonging to the government of a\ncountry is taken to have been born in that country.\nPersons born after death of parent\n\n(2) For the purposes of this Act, the status of a parent of a person at the\ntime of the person’s birth is, for a parent who died before the birth,\ntaken to be the status of the parent when the parent died.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-7-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-7-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "75ddca66e41f6a3fc284c101744d91a5eb83a7b5e1caa14b936e2b6ce2488e2a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "7 Children born on ships or aircraft or after death of parent",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 18,
      "values:originalText": "Persons born on ships or aircraft\n\n(1) For the purposes of this Act:\n\n(a) a person born on a ship or aircraft registered in Australia or a\nforeign country is taken to have been born at the place at\nwhich the ship or aircraft is registered; and\n\n(b) a person born on a ship or aircraft not registered in Australia\nor a foreign country and belonging to the government of a\ncountry is taken to have been born in that country.\nPersons born after death of parent\n\n(2) For the purposes of this Act, the status of a parent of a person at the\ntime of the person’s birth is, for a parent who died before the birth,\ntaken to be the status of the parent when the parent died."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-7-ss-1",
