    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-8",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "8 Children born as a result of artificial conception procedures or",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-8"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf, p.18",
      "values:originalText": "surrogacy arrangements\n\n(1) This section applies if a child is:\n\n(a) a child of a person under section 60H or 60HB of the Family\nLaw Act 1975; and\n\n(b) either:\n\n(i) a child of the person’s spouse or de facto partner under\nthat section; or\n\n(ii) a biological child of the person’s spouse\nor de facto partner.\n\n(2) The child is taken for the purposes of this Act:\n\n(a) to be the child of the person and the spouse\nor de facto partner; and\n\n(b) not to be the child of anyone else.\n\n\nPreliminary  Part 1\n\nSection 9\n\nAustralian Citizenship Act 2007\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "skos:definition": "surrogacy arrangements\n\n(1) This section applies if a child is:\n\n(a) a child of a person under section 60H or 60HB of the Family\nLaw Act 1975; and\n\n(b) either:\n\n(i) a child of the person’s spouse or de facto partner under\nthat section; or\n\n(ii) a biological child of the person’s spouse\nor de facto partner.\n\n(2) The child is taken for the purposes of this Act:\n\n(a) to be the child of the person and the spouse\nor de facto partner; and\n\n(b) not to be the child of anyone else.\n\n\nPreliminary  Part 1\n\nSection 9\n\nAustralian Citizenship Act 2007\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-8-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-8-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "aba46aea5b94ce6978f5a7033db6bc3c704a5d86d0038b2f6a5740701ce4a423"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-8",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "8 Children born as a result of artificial conception procedures or",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 18,
      "values:originalText": "surrogacy arrangements\n\n(1) This section applies if a child is:\n\n(a) a child of a person under section 60H or 60HB of the Family\nLaw Act 1975; and\n\n(b) either:\n\n(i) a child of the person’s spouse or de facto partner under\nthat section; or\n\n(ii) a biological child of the person’s spouse\nor de facto partner.\n\n(2) The child is taken for the purposes of this Act:\n\n(a) to be the child of the person and the spouse\nor de facto partner; and\n\n(b) not to be the child of anyone else.\n\n\nPreliminary  Part 1\n\nSection 9\n\nAustralian Citizenship Act 2007\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026"
    },
