      "cml:premiseText": "(3) For the purposes of this Act, the period during which a person is\nconfined in a psychiatric institution by order of a court includes a\nperiod during which the person is an escapee from the institution.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The period during which a person is confined in a psychiatric institution by order of a court overlaps with the period during which the person is an escapee from the institution."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-10",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10 Personal identifiers",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-10"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf, p.19",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, a personal identifier is any of the\nfollowing (including any of the following in digital form):\n\n(a) fingerprints or handprints of a person (including those taken\nusing paper and ink or digital livescanning technologies);\n\n(b) a measurement of a person’s height and weight;\n\n(c) a photograph or other image of a person’s face;\nNote:\nSee section 10A.\n\n(d) an iris scan;\n\n(e) a person’s signature;\n\n(f) any other identifier prescribed by the regulations (except an\nidentifier the obtaining of which would involve the carrying\nout of an intimate forensic procedure within the meaning of\nsection 23WA of the Crimes Act 1914).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Act, a personal identifier is any of the\nfollowing (including any of the following in digital form):\n\n(a) fingerprints or handprints of a person (including those taken\nusing paper and ink or digital livescanning technologies);\n\n(b) a measurement of a person’s height and weight;\n\n(c) a photograph or other image of a person’s face;\nNote:\nSee section 10A.\n\n(d) an iris scan;\n\n(e) a person’s signature;\n\n(f) any other identifier prescribed by the regulations (except an\nidentifier the obtaining of which would involve the carrying\nout of an intimate forensic procedure within the meaning of\nsection 23WA of the Crimes Act 1914).",
