      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf, p.23",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person born in Australia is an Australian citizen if and only if:\n\n(a) a parent of the person is an Australian citizen, or a permanent\nresident, at the time the person is born; or\n\n(b) the person is ordinarily resident in Australia throughout the\nperiod of 10 years beginning on the day the person is born.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person born in Australia is an Australian citizen if and only if:\n\n(a) a parent of the person is an Australian citizen, or a permanent\nresident, at the time the person is born; or\n\n(b) the person is ordinarily resident in Australia throughout the\nperiod of 10 years beginning on the day the person is born.",
      "cml:asserts": [
