    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-15-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15 Citizenship by incorporation of Territory",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-15-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person is an Australian citizen if:\n\n(a) any territory becomes a part of Australia; and\n\n(b) the person is included in a class of persons specified in a\ndetermination under this section.\nDetermination\n\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that\nspecified classes of persons are Australian citizens from a specified\nday because of their connection with that territory.\n\n\nAustralian citizenship  Part 2\nAutomatic acquisition of Australian citizenship  Division 1\n\nSection 15\n\nAustralian Citizenship Act 2007\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nDay citizenship begins\n\n(3) The person becomes an Australian citizen on that day.\nRetrospective application of instruments\n\n(4) Subsection 12(2) (retrospective application of legislative\ninstruments) of the Legislation Act 2003 does not apply to the\ninstrument.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person is an Australian citizen if:\n\n(a) any territory becomes a part of Australia; and\n\n(b) the person is included in a class of persons specified in a\ndetermination under this section.\nDetermination\n\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that\nspecified classes of persons are Australian citizens from a specified\nday because of their connection with that territory.\n\n\nAustralian citizenship  Part 2\nAutomatic acquisition of Australian citizenship  Division 1\n\nSection 15\n\nAustralian Citizenship Act 2007\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nDay citizenship begins\n\n(3) The person becomes an Australian citizen on that day.\nRetrospective application of instruments\n\n(4) Subsection 12(2) (retrospective application of legislative\ninstruments) of the Legislation Act 2003 does not apply to the\ninstrument.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-15-2-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-15-2-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-15-2-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-15-2-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "faea5fc5352aa4e028c9425f77a66b4ee947b28956a20a10b4e0af668c5af2fd"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-15-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15 Citizenship by incorporation of Territory",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 24,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person is an Australian citizen if:\n\n(a) any territory becomes a part of Australia; and\n\n(b) the person is included in a class of persons specified in a\ndetermination under this section.\nDetermination\n\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine that\nspecified classes of persons are Australian citizens from a specified\nday because of their connection with that territory.\n\n\nAustralian citizenship  Part 2\nAutomatic acquisition of Australian citizenship  Division 1\n\nSection 15\n\nAustralian Citizenship Act 2007\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nDay citizenship begins\n\n(3) The person becomes an Australian citizen on that day.\nRetrospective application of instruments\n\n(4) Subsection 12(2) (retrospective application of legislative\ninstruments) of the Legislation Act 2003 does not apply to the\ninstrument."
    },
