    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-19d-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "19D(5) Minister’s decision",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-19d-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf, p.33",
      "values:originalText": "(5) If the person is not covered by subsection (7), the Minister must\nnot approve the person becoming an Australian citizen at a time\nwhen an adverse security assessment, or a qualified security\nassessment, in respect of the person is in force under the Australian\nSecurity Intelligence Organisation Act 1979 that the person is\ndirectly or indirectly a risk to security (within the meaning of\nsection 4 of that Act).",
      "skos:definition": "(5) If the person is not covered by subsection (7), the Minister must\nnot approve the person becoming an Australian citizen at a time\nwhen an adverse security assessment, or a qualified security\nassessment, in respect of the person is in force under the Australian\nSecurity Intelligence Organisation Act 1979 that the person is\ndirectly or indirectly a risk to security (within the meaning of\nsection 4 of that Act).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-19d"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-19d-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-19d-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9b05a85dad7a148e0f5d9524b1ad232c24dc490b4e1ca7dba868d49d9b596cbf",
      "skos:note": "Minister must not approve citizenship if person is a security risk."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-19d-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "19D(5) Minister’s decision",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 33,
      "values:originalText": "(5) If the person is not covered by subsection (7), the Minister must\nnot approve the person becoming an Australian citizen at a time\nwhen an adverse security assessment, or a qualified security\nassessment, in respect of the person is in force under the Australian\nSecurity Intelligence Organisation Act 1979 that the person is\ndirectly or indirectly a risk to security (within the meaning of\nsection 4 of that Act)."
    },
    {
