      "cml:integrityHash": "a65fd4eba6fa19e4315a298e1ba41f0fecfd381c35b0ccc1eb61f596bd859a4e",
      "skos:note": "General residence requirement for permanent residency application"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-22-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "22(1) General residence requirement",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 41,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to this section, for the purposes of section 21 a person\nsatisfies the general residence requirement if:\n\n(a) the person was present in Australia for the period of 4 years\nimmediately before the day the person made the application;\nand\n\n(b) the person was not present in Australia as an unlawful\nnon-citizen at any time during that 4 year period; and\n\n(c) the person was present in Australia as a permanent resident\nfor the period of 12 months immediately before the day the\nperson made the application.\nOverseas absences"
    },
