    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-24",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "24 Minister’s decision",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-24"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf, p.55",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a person makes an application under section 21, the Minister\nmust, by writing, approve or refuse to approve the person\nbecoming an Australian citizen.\nNote:\nThe Minister may cancel an approval: see section 25.\n\n(1A) The Minister must not approve the person becoming an Australian\ncitizen unless the person is eligible to become an Australian citizen\nunder subsection 21(2), (3), (4), (5), (6), (7) or (8).\n\n(2) The Minister may refuse to approve the person becoming an\nAustralian citizen despite the person being eligible to become an\nAustralian citizen under subsection 21(2), (3), (4), (5), (6) or (7).\n\n(2A) If the Minister exercised the power under subsection 22A(1A) or\n22B(1A) in relation to the person, the decision under subsection (1)\nof this section must be made by the Minister personally.\nIdentity\n\n(3) The Minister must not approve the person becoming an Australian\ncitizen unless the Minister is satisfied of the identity of the person.\nNote:\nDivision 5 contains the identity provisions.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a person makes an application under section 21, the Minister\nmust, by writing, approve or refuse to approve the person\nbecoming an Australian citizen.\nNote:\nThe Minister may cancel an approval: see section 25.\n\n(1A) The Minister must not approve the person becoming an Australian\ncitizen unless the person is eligible to become an Australian citizen\nunder subsection 21(2), (3), (4), (5), (6), (7) or (8).\n\n(2) The Minister may refuse to approve the person becoming an\nAustralian citizen despite the person being eligible to become an\nAustralian citizen under subsection 21(2), (3), (4), (5), (6) or (7).\n\n(2A) If the Minister exercised the power under subsection 22A(1A) or\n22B(1A) in relation to the person, the decision under subsection (1)\nof this section must be made by the Minister personally.\nIdentity\n\n(3) The Minister must not approve the person becoming an Australian\ncitizen unless the Minister is satisfied of the identity of the person.\nNote:\nDivision 5 contains the identity provisions.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-24-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-24-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-24-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-24-ss-2a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-24-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e14b7fa3fd943431cb719b9def25c8b7e4a087365e972059705ba68ba61dcbc8"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-24",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "24 Minister’s decision",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 55,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a person makes an application under section 21, the Minister\nmust, by writing, approve or refuse to approve the person\nbecoming an Australian citizen.\nNote:\nThe Minister may cancel an approval: see section 25.\n\n(1A) The Minister must not approve the person becoming an Australian\ncitizen unless the person is eligible to become an Australian citizen\nunder subsection 21(2), (3), (4), (5), (6), (7) or (8).\n\n(2) The Minister may refuse to approve the person becoming an\nAustralian citizen despite the person being eligible to become an\nAustralian citizen under subsection 21(2), (3), (4), (5), (6) or (7).\n\n(2A) If the Minister exercised the power under subsection 22A(1A) or\n22B(1A) in relation to the person, the decision under subsection (1)\nof this section must be made by the Minister personally.\nIdentity\n\n(3) The Minister must not approve the person becoming an Australian\ncitizen unless the Minister is satisfied of the identity of the person.\nNote:\nDivision 5 contains the identity provisions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-24-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "24(1) Minister’s decision",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
