      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3) A person is eligible to become an Australian citizen again under this Subdivision if:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-30",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "30 Minister’s decision",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-30"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf, p.65",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a person makes an application under section 29, the Minister\nmust, by writing, approve or refuse to approve the person\nbecoming an Australian citizen again.\n\n(1A) The Minister must not approve the person becoming an Australian\ncitizen again unless the person is eligible to become an Australian\ncitizen again under subsection 29(2) or (3).\n\n(2) The Minister may refuse to approve the person becoming an\nAustralian citizen again despite the person being eligible to\nbecome an Australian citizen again under subsection 29(2) or (3).\nIdentity\n\n(3) The Minister must not approve the person becoming an Australian\ncitizen again unless the Minister is satisfied of the identity of the\nperson.\nNote:\nDivision 5 contains the identity provisions.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a person makes an application under section 29, the Minister\nmust, by writing, approve or refuse to approve the person\nbecoming an Australian citizen again.\n\n(1A) The Minister must not approve the person becoming an Australian\ncitizen again unless the person is eligible to become an Australian\ncitizen again under subsection 29(2) or (3).\n\n(2) The Minister may refuse to approve the person becoming an\nAustralian citizen again despite the person being eligible to\nbecome an Australian citizen again under subsection 29(2) or (3).\nIdentity\n\n(3) The Minister must not approve the person becoming an Australian\ncitizen again unless the Minister is satisfied of the identity of the\nperson.\nNote:\nDivision 5 contains the identity provisions.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-30-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-30-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-30-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-30-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e7ac943c87ce2393e3a87e64d49ba108a1b679891fa09227ee73749c20b9658a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-30",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "30 Minister’s decision",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 65,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a person makes an application under section 29, the Minister\nmust, by writing, approve or refuse to approve the person\nbecoming an Australian citizen again.\n\n(1A) The Minister must not approve the person becoming an Australian\ncitizen again unless the person is eligible to become an Australian\ncitizen again under subsection 29(2) or (3).\n\n(2) The Minister may refuse to approve the person becoming an\nAustralian citizen again despite the person being eligible to\nbecome an Australian citizen again under subsection 29(2) or (3).\nIdentity\n\n(3) The Minister must not approve the person becoming an Australian\ncitizen again unless the Minister is satisfied of the identity of the\nperson.\nNote:\nDivision 5 contains the identity provisions."
    },
