    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-33",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "33 Renunciation by application",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-33"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf, p.69",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person may make an application to the Minister to renounce the\nperson’s Australian citizenship.\nNote:\nSection 46 sets out application requirements (which may include the\npayment of a fee).\nMinister’s decision\n\n(2) The Minister must, by writing, approve or refuse to approve the\nperson renouncing his or her Australian citizenship.\n\n(3) Subject to this section, the Minister must approve the person\nrenouncing his or her Australian citizenship if the Minister is\nsatisfied that:\n\n(a) the person is aged 18 or over, and is a national or citizen of a\nforeign country, at the time the person made the application;\nor\n\n(b) the person was born, or is ordinarily resident, in a foreign\ncountry and is not entitled, under the law of that country, to\nacquire the nationality or citizenship of that country because\nthe person is an Australian citizen.\n\n(4) The Minister must not approve the person renouncing his or her\nAustralian citizenship unless the Minister is satisfied of the identity\nof the person.\nNote:\nDivision 5 contains the identity provisions.\n\n(5) The Minister may refuse to approve the person renouncing his or\nher Australian citizenship if the person:\n\n(a) is a national or citizen of a foreign country at the time the\nperson made the application; and\n\n(b) made the application during a war in which Australia is\nengaged.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person may make an application to the Minister to renounce the\nperson’s Australian citizenship.\nNote:\nSection 46 sets out application requirements (which may include the\npayment of a fee).\nMinister’s decision\n\n(2) The Minister must, by writing, approve or refuse to approve the\nperson renouncing his or her Australian citizenship.\n\n(3) Subject to this section, the Minister must approve the person\nrenouncing his or her Australian citizenship if the Minister is\nsatisfied that:\n\n(a) the person is aged 18 or over, and is a national or citizen of a\nforeign country, at the time the person made the application;\nor\n\n(b) the person was born, or is ordinarily resident, in a foreign\ncountry and is not entitled, under the law of that country, to\nacquire the nationality or citizenship of that country because\nthe person is an Australian citizen.\n\n(4) The Minister must not approve the person renouncing his or her\nAustralian citizenship unless the Minister is satisfied of the identity\nof the person.\nNote:\nDivision 5 contains the identity provisions.\n\n(5) The Minister may refuse to approve the person renouncing his or\nher Australian citizenship if the person:\n\n(a) is a national or citizen of a foreign country at the time the\nperson made the application; and\n\n(b) made the application during a war in which Australia is\nengaged.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-33-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-33-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-33-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-33-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-33-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3bbd2b493505acbedc35a7ee5eb841c736a03d3801d7921193d664e4d978f582"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-33",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "33 Renunciation by application",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 69,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person may make an application to the Minister to renounce the\nperson’s Australian citizenship.\nNote:\nSection 46 sets out application requirements (which may include the\npayment of a fee).\nMinister’s decision\n\n(2) The Minister must, by writing, approve or refuse to approve the\nperson renouncing his or her Australian citizenship.\n\n(3) Subject to this section, the Minister must approve the person\nrenouncing his or her Australian citizenship if the Minister is\nsatisfied that:\n\n(a) the person is aged 18 or over, and is a national or citizen of a\nforeign country, at the time the person made the application;\nor\n\n(b) the person was born, or is ordinarily resident, in a foreign\ncountry and is not entitled, under the law of that country, to\nacquire the nationality or citizenship of that country because\nthe person is an Australian citizen.\n\n(4) The Minister must not approve the person renouncing his or her\nAustralian citizenship unless the Minister is satisfied of the identity\nof the person.\nNote:\nDivision 5 contains the identity provisions.\n\n(5) The Minister may refuse to approve the person renouncing his or\nher Australian citizenship if the person:\n\n(a) is a national or citizen of a foreign country at the time the\nperson made the application; and\n\n(b) made the application during a war in which Australia is\nengaged."
    },
