      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf, p.73",
      "values:originalText": "other person committed at any time before the Minister gave\nthe approval; and\n\n(b) the act or omission that constituted the offence was\nconnected with the Minister approving the applicant\nbecoming an Australian citizen.\nCharge proved but no conviction\n\n(9) A reference in this section to a conviction of an offence:\n\n(a) in relation to a law of the Commonwealth—includes a\nreference to the making of an order under section 19B of the\nCrimes Act 1914 in relation to the offence; and\n\n(b) in relation to a law of a State or Territory or a foreign\ncountry—includes a reference to the making of an order\nunder the corresponding provision of a law of the State or\nTerritory or foreign country in relation to the offence.",
      "skos:definition": "other person committed at any time before the Minister gave\nthe approval; and\n\n(b) the act or omission that constituted the offence was\nconnected with the Minister approving the applicant\nbecoming an Australian citizen.\nCharge proved but no conviction\n\n(9) A reference in this section to a conviction of an offence:\n\n(a) in relation to a law of the Commonwealth—includes a\nreference to the making of an order under section 19B of the\nCrimes Act 1914 in relation to the offence; and\n\n(b) in relation to a law of a State or Territory or a foreign\ncountry—includes a reference to the making of an order\nunder the corresponding provision of a law of the State or\nTerritory or foreign country in relation to the offence.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-145-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-145-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-145-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-145-logic-alleninterval-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7843dae8f49a829532fc9d671681204e90a12c4086e3e6ee0c62ad3eea74351e",
      "skos:note": "The Minister must approve an applicant becoming an Australian citizen before a conviction can be referred to the court."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-145",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "145 2, 145.4, 145.5 or 149.1 of the Criminal Code, that the",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 73,
      "values:originalText": "other person committed at any time before the Minister gave\nthe approval; and\n\n(b) the act or omission that constituted the offence was\nconnected with the Minister approving the applicant\nbecoming an Australian citizen.\nCharge proved but no conviction\n\n(9) A reference in this section to a conviction of an offence:\n\n(a) in relation to a law of the Commonwealth—includes a\nreference to the making of an order under section 19B of the\nCrimes Act 1914 in relation to the offence; and\n\n(b) in relation to a law of a State or Territory or a foreign\ncountry—includes a reference to the making of an order\nunder the corresponding provision of a law of the State or\nTerritory or foreign country in relation to the offence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-145-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
