    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-36",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "36 Children of responsible parents who cease to be citizens",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-36"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf, p.74",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n\nAustralian citizenship  Part 2\nCessation of Australian citizenship  Division 3\n\nSection 36A\n\nAustralian Citizenship Act 2007\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) a person ceases to be an Australian citizen at a particular time\n(the cessation time) under section 33, 34 or 34A; and\n\n(b) at the cessation time, the person is a responsible parent of a\nchild aged under 18;\nthen:\n\n(c) the Minister may, by writing, revoke the child’s Australian\ncitizenship; and\n\n(d) if the Minister does so—the child ceases to be an Australian\ncitizen at the time of the revocation.\nException—another responsible parent\n\n(2) If, at the cessation time, another responsible parent of the child is\nan Australian citizen, subsection (1) does not apply to the child:\n\n(a) while there is a responsible parent who is an Australian\ncitizen; and\n\n(b) if there ceases to be such a responsible parent because of the\ndeath of a responsible parent—at any time after that death.\nException—statelessness\n\n(3) The Minister must not revoke a child’s Australian citizenship\nunder subsection (1) if the Minister is satisfied that the child would\nthen become a person who is not a national or citizen of any\ncountry.\nSubdivision C—Citizenship cessation",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n\n\nAustralian citizenship  Part 2\nCessation of Australian citizenship  Division 3\n\nSection 36A\n\nAustralian Citizenship Act 2007\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) a person ceases to be an Australian citizen at a particular time\n(the cessation time) under section 33, 34 or 34A; and\n\n(b) at the cessation time, the person is a responsible parent of a\nchild aged under 18;\nthen:\n\n(c) the Minister may, by writing, revoke the child’s Australian\ncitizenship; and\n\n(d) if the Minister does so—the child ceases to be an Australian\ncitizen at the time of the revocation.\nException—another responsible parent\n\n(2) If, at the cessation time, another responsible parent of the child is\nan Australian citizen, subsection (1) does not apply to the child:\n\n(a) while there is a responsible parent who is an Australian\ncitizen; and\n\n(b) if there ceases to be such a responsible parent because of the\ndeath of a responsible parent—at any time after that death.\nException—statelessness\n\n(3) The Minister must not revoke a child’s Australian citizenship\nunder subsection (1) if the Minister is satisfied that the child would\nthen become a person who is not a national or citizen of any\ncountry.\nSubdivision C—Citizenship cessation",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-36-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-36-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-36-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "10378cc8ac6995a3163285ac7aa7f7c85fb4220b5cc994e633fb5f8f696d14ba"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-36",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "36 Children of responsible parents who cease to be citizens",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 74,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n\n\nAustralian citizenship  Part 2\nCessation of Australian citizenship  Division 3\n\nSection 36A\n\nAustralian Citizenship Act 2007\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(a) a person ceases to be an Australian citizen at a particular time\n(the cessation time) under section 33, 34 or 34A; and\n\n(b) at the cessation time, the person is a responsible parent of a\nchild aged under 18;\nthen:\n\n(c) the Minister may, by writing, revoke the child’s Australian\ncitizenship; and\n\n(d) if the Minister does so—the child ceases to be an Australian\ncitizen at the time of the revocation.\nException—another responsible parent\n\n(2) If, at the cessation time, another responsible parent of the child is\nan Australian citizen, subsection (1) does not apply to the child:\n\n(a) while there is a responsible parent who is an Australian\ncitizen; and\n\n(b) if there ceases to be such a responsible parent because of the\ndeath of a responsible parent—at any time after that death.\nException—statelessness\n\n(3) The Minister must not revoke a child’s Australian citizenship\nunder subsection (1) if the Minister is satisfied that the child would\nthen become a person who is not a national or citizen of any\ncountry.\nSubdivision C—Citizenship cessation"
    },
    {
