    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-36c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "36C Citizenship cessation order if person is convicted of serious",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-36c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf, p.76",
      "values:originalText": "offence\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) a person is convicted of one or more serious offences; and\n\n(b) the court has decided to impose on the person, in respect of\nthe conviction or convictions, a period of imprisonment that\nis at least 3 years or periods of imprisonment that total at\nleast 3 years; and\n\n\nAustralian citizenship  Part 2\nCessation of Australian citizenship  Division 3\n\nSection 36C\n\nAustralian Citizenship Act 2007\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(c) before the court imposes the sentence or sentences on the\nperson in respect of the conviction or convictions, the\nMinister makes an application under subsection 36D(1) for\nan order to be made under this subsection in relation to the\nperson; and\n\n(d) the court is satisfied of the matters specified in subsection (4)\nof this section;\nthe court may, when imposing such a period or periods of\nimprisonment on the person in respect of the conviction or\nconvictions, also order at that time as part of the sentence or\nsentences that the person ceases to be an Australian citizen.\nNote:\nSubsections (5) and (6) set out, without limitation, matters the court\nmust have regard to in deciding whether to make an order under this\nsubsection.\n\n(2) However, the court must not make an order under subsection (1) in\nrelation to the person if the court is satisfied that the person would,\nif the court were to make the order, become a person who is not a\nnational or citizen of any country.\nSerious offence\n\n(3) A serious offence is an offence against any of the following\nprovisions:\n\n(a) a provision of Subdivision A of Division 72 of the Criminal\nCode (explosives and lethal devices);\n\n(b) a provision of Subdivision B of Division 80 of the Criminal\nCode (treason);\n\n(c) section 83.1 of the Criminal Code (advocating mutiny);\n\n(d) a provision of Division 91 of the Criminal Code (espionage);\n\n(e) a provision of Division 92 of the Criminal Code (foreign\ninterference);\n\n(f) a provision of Part 5.3 of the Criminal Code (terrorism),\nother than the following provisions:\n\n(i) section 102.8;\n\n(ii) Division 104;\n\n(iii) Division 105;",
      "skos:definition": "offence\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) a person is convicted of one or more serious offences; and\n\n(b) the court has decided to impose on the person, in respect of\nthe conviction or convictions, a period of imprisonment that\nis at least 3 years or periods of imprisonment that total at\nleast 3 years; and\n\n\nAustralian citizenship  Part 2\nCessation of Australian citizenship  Division 3\n\nSection 36C\n\nAustralian Citizenship Act 2007\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(c) before the court imposes the sentence or sentences on the\nperson in respect of the conviction or convictions, the\nMinister makes an application under subsection 36D(1) for\nan order to be made under this subsection in relation to the\nperson; and\n\n(d) the court is satisfied of the matters specified in subsection (4)\nof this section;\nthe court may, when imposing such a period or periods of\nimprisonment on the person in respect of the conviction or\nconvictions, also order at that time as part of the sentence or\nsentences that the person ceases to be an Australian citizen.\nNote:\nSubsections (5) and (6) set out, without limitation, matters the court\nmust have regard to in deciding whether to make an order under this\nsubsection.\n\n(2) However, the court must not make an order under subsection (1) in\nrelation to the person if the court is satisfied that the person would,\nif the court were to make the order, become a person who is not a\nnational or citizen of any country.\nSerious offence\n\n(3) A serious offence is an offence against any of the following\nprovisions:\n\n(a) a provision of Subdivision A of Division 72 of the Criminal\nCode (explosives and lethal devices);\n\n(b) a provision of Subdivision B of Division 80 of the Criminal\nCode (treason);\n\n(c) section 83.1 of the Criminal Code (advocating mutiny);\n\n(d) a provision of Division 91 of the Criminal Code (espionage);\n\n(e) a provision of Division 92 of the Criminal Code (foreign\ninterference);\n\n(f) a provision of Part 5.3 of the Criminal Code (terrorism),\nother than the following prov",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-36c-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-36c-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-36c-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "dd04d87829718f9c48780788259f9efb877c778151671a62aee54d384826e663"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-36c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "36C Citizenship cessation order if person is convicted of serious",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 76,
      "values:originalText": "offence\n\n(1) If:\n\n(a) a person is convicted of one or more serious offences; and\n\n(b) the court has decided to impose on the person, in respect of\nthe conviction or convictions, a period of imprisonment that\nis at least 3 years or periods of imprisonment that total at\nleast 3 years; and\n\n\nAustralian citizenship  Part 2\nCessation of Australian citizenship  Division 3\n\nSection 36C\n\nAustralian Citizenship Act 2007\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\n(c) before the court imposes the sentence or sentences on the\nperson in respect of the conviction or convictions, the\nMinister makes an application under subsection 36D(1) for\nan order to be made under this subsection in relation to the\nperson; and\n\n(d) the court is satisfied of the matters specified in subsection (4)\nof this section;\nthe court may, when imposing such a period or periods of\nimprisonment on the person in respect of the conviction or\nconvictions, also order at that time as part of the sentence or\nsentences that the person ceases to be an Australian citizen.\nNote:\nSubsections (5) and (6) set out, without limitation, matters the court\nmust have regard to in deciding whether to make an order under this\nsubsection.\n\n(2) However, the court must not make an order under subsection (1) in\nrelation to the person if the court is satisfied that the person would,\nif the court were to make the order, become a person who is not a\nnational or citizen of any country.\nSerious offence\n\n(3) A serious offence is an offence against any of the following\nprovisions:\n\n(a) a provision of Subdivision A of Division 72 of the Criminal\nCode (explosives and lethal devices);\n\n(b) a provision of Subdivision B of Division 80 of the Criminal\nCode (treason);\n\n(c) section 83.1 of the Criminal Code (advocating mutiny);\n\n(d) a provision of Division 91 of the Criminal Code (espionage);\n\n(e) a provision of Division 92 of the Criminal Code (foreign\ninterference);\n\n(f) a provision of Part 5.3 of the Criminal Code (terrorism),\nother than the following provisions:\n\n(i) section 102.8;\n\n(ii) Division 104;\n\n(iii) Division 105;"
    },
