    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-43",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "43 Disclosing identifying information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-43"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf, p.87",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person’s conduct causes disclosure of identifying\ninformation; and\n\n(b) the disclosure is not a permitted disclosure.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years, or 120 penalty units, or both.\n\n(1A) If:\n\n(a) a disclosure of identifying information is made to a person\nwho is not an entrusted person; and\n\n(b) the disclosure is a permitted disclosure;\nthis section does not apply in relation to any further disclosure of\nthat identifying information by a person who is not an entrusted\nperson.\nNote 1:\nA defendant, except for an IGIS official, bears an evidential burden in\nrelation to a matter in this subsection (see subsection 13.3(3) of the\nCriminal Code). For IGIS officials, see section 34C of the\nInspector-General of Intelligence and Security Act 1986.\nNote 2:\nAustralian Privacy Principle 6 may apply to further disclosures of that\nidentifying information by a person who is not an entrusted person.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person’s conduct causes disclosure of identifying\ninformation; and\n\n(b) the disclosure is not a permitted disclosure.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years, or 120 penalty units, or both.\n\n(1A) If:\n\n(a) a disclosure of identifying information is made to a person\nwho is not an entrusted person; and\n\n(b) the disclosure is a permitted disclosure;\nthis section does not apply in relation to any further disclosure of\nthat identifying information by a person who is not an entrusted\nperson.\nNote 1:\nA defendant, except for an IGIS official, bears an evidential burden in\nrelation to a matter in this subsection (see subsection 13.3(3) of the\nCriminal Code). For IGIS officials, see section 34C of the\nInspector-General of Intelligence and Security Act 1986.\nNote 2:\nAustralian Privacy Principle 6 may apply to further disclosures of that\nidentifying information by a person who is not an entrusted person.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-43-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-43-ss-1a"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9b0273cbc1b45b8550397aaec26982cc0fc9417f4f41dfb1b2810b58dc0bcee6"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-43",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "43 Disclosing identifying information",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 87,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person’s conduct causes disclosure of identifying\ninformation; and\n\n(b) the disclosure is not a permitted disclosure.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years, or 120 penalty units, or both.\n\n(1A) If:\n\n(a) a disclosure of identifying information is made to a person\nwho is not an entrusted person; and\n\n(b) the disclosure is a permitted disclosure;\nthis section does not apply in relation to any further disclosure of\nthat identifying information by a person who is not an entrusted\nperson.\nNote 1:\nA defendant, except for an IGIS official, bears an evidential burden in\nrelation to a matter in this subsection (see subsection 13.3(3) of the\nCriminal Code). For IGIS officials, see section 34C of the\nInspector-General of Intelligence and Security Act 1986.\nNote 2:\nAustralian Privacy Principle 6 may apply to further disclosures of that\nidentifying information by a person who is not an entrusted person."
    },
