    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-44",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44 Unauthorised modification or impairment of identifying",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-44"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf, p.89",
      "values:originalText": "information\nUnauthorised modification\n\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person causes any unauthorised modification of\nidentifying information; and\n\n(b) the person intends to cause the modification; and\n\n(c) the person knows that the modification is unauthorised.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years, or 120 penalty units, or both.\nUnauthorised impairment\n\n(2) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person causes any unauthorised impairment of:\n\n(i) the reliability of identifying information; or\n\n(ii) the security of the storage of identifying information; or\n\n(iii) the operation of a system by which identifying\ninformation is stored; and\n\n(b) the person intends to cause the impairment; and\n\n(c) the person knows that the impairment is unauthorised.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years, or 120 penalty units, or both.\nException\n\n(2A) If:\n\n(a) a disclosure of identifying information is made to a person\nwho is not an entrusted person; and\n\n(b) the disclosure is a permitted disclosure within the meaning of\nsection 43;\nthis section does not apply in relation to any modification or\nimpairment of that identifying information by a person who is not\nan entrusted person.",
      "skos:definition": "information\nUnauthorised modification\n\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person causes any unauthorised modification of\nidentifying information; and\n\n(b) the person intends to cause the modification; and\n\n(c) the person knows that the modification is unauthorised.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years, or 120 penalty units, or both.\nUnauthorised impairment\n\n(2) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person causes any unauthorised impairment of:\n\n(i) the reliability of identifying information; or\n\n(ii) the security of the storage of identifying information; or\n\n(iii) the operation of a system by which identifying\ninformation is stored; and\n\n(b) the person intends to cause the impairment; and\n\n(c) the person knows that the impairment is unauthorised.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years, or 120 penalty units, or both.\nException\n\n(2A) If:\n\n(a) a disclosure of identifying information is made to a person\nwho is not an entrusted person; and\n\n(b) the disclosure is a permitted disclosure within the meaning of\nsection 43;\nthis section does not apply in relation to any modification or\nimpairment of that identifying information by a person who is not\nan entrusted person.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-44-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-44-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-44-ss-2a"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f028bb612c987b72473abd092c9e474e6238e02301910db493eea8e17841a789"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-44",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44 Unauthorised modification or impairment of identifying",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 89,
      "values:originalText": "information\nUnauthorised modification\n\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person causes any unauthorised modification of\nidentifying information; and\n\n(b) the person intends to cause the modification; and\n\n(c) the person knows that the modification is unauthorised.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years, or 120 penalty units, or both.\nUnauthorised impairment\n\n(2) A person commits an offence if:\n\n(a) the person causes any unauthorised impairment of:\n\n(i) the reliability of identifying information; or\n\n(ii) the security of the storage of identifying information; or\n\n(iii) the operation of a system by which identifying\ninformation is stored; and\n\n(b) the person intends to cause the impairment; and\n\n(c) the person knows that the impairment is unauthorised.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years, or 120 penalty units, or both.\nException\n\n(2A) If:\n\n(a) a disclosure of identifying information is made to a person\nwho is not an entrusted person; and\n\n(b) the disclosure is a permitted disclosure within the meaning of\nsection 43;\nthis section does not apply in relation to any modification or\nimpairment of that identifying information by a person who is not\nan entrusted person."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-44-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44(1) Unauthorised modification or impairment of identifying",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-44-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
