      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf, p.93",
      "values:originalText": "(5) For the purposes of subsection (4), if the proceedings go to\njudgment, they end:\n\n(a) if no appeal against the judgment is lodged within the period\nfor lodging such an appeal—at the end of that period; or",
      "skos:definition": "(5) For the purposes of subsection (4), if the proceedings go to\njudgment, they end:\n\n(a) if no appeal against the judgment is lodged within the period\nfor lodging such an appeal—at the end of that period; or",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-45c"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
