    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-46",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "46 Application requirements",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-46"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf, p.95",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An application under a provision of this Act must:\n\n(a) be on the relevant form approved by the Minister for the\npurposes of that provision; and\n\n(b) contain the information required by the form; and\n\n(c) be accompanied by any other information or documents\nprescribed by the regulations; and\n\n(d) be accompanied by the fee (if any) prescribed by the\nregulations.\n\n(1AA) However, paragraphs (1)(a) and (b) do not apply to an application\nmade under section 37 (evidence of Australian citizenship) if the\napplication:\n\n(a) is made in a manner prescribed by the regulations; and\n\n(b) contains the information prescribed by the regulations.\n\n(1A) For applications made under section 21 by persons who, in order to\nbe eligible to become an Australian citizen under subsection 21(2),\nmust have sat a test approved in a determination under\nsection 23A, the fee prescribed by the regulations may include a\ncomponent that relates to the sitting of that test.\nApproval of forms\n\n(2) The Minister may, by writing, approve one or more forms for the\npurposes of a provision of this Act under which an application may\nbe made.\nNote:\nFor example, there are 2 ways to become an Australian citizen by\ndescent under section 16. The Minister may approve 1 form for the\npurposes of that section or may approve 2 different forms.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An application under a provision of this Act must:\n\n(a) be on the relevant form approved by the Minister for the\npurposes of that provision; and\n\n(b) contain the information required by the form; and\n\n(c) be accompanied by any other information or documents\nprescribed by the regulations; and\n\n(d) be accompanied by the fee (if any) prescribed by the\nregulations.\n\n(1AA) However, paragraphs (1)(a) and (b) do not apply to an application\nmade under section 37 (evidence of Australian citizenship) if the\napplication:\n\n(a) is made in a manner prescribed by the regulations; and\n\n(b) contains the information prescribed by the regulations.\n\n(1A) For applications made under section 21 by persons who, in order to\nbe eligible to become an Australian citizen under subsection 21(2),\nmust have sat a test approved in a determination under\nsection 23A, the fee prescribed by the regulations may include a\ncomponent that relates to the sitting of that test.\nApproval of forms\n\n(2) The Minister may, by writing, approve one or more forms for the\npurposes of a provision of this Act under which an application may\nbe made.\nNote:\nFor example, there are 2 ways to become an Australian citizen by\ndescent under section 16. The Minister may approve 1 form for the\npurposes of that section or may approve 2 different forms.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-46-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-46-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-46-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b3b9505fbe0365bb1c7b86491c021b1cc31f9b9bd136d9259c471e19d8f97ccc"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-46",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "46 Application requirements",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 95,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An application under a provision of this Act must:\n\n(a) be on the relevant form approved by the Minister for the\npurposes of that provision; and\n\n(b) contain the information required by the form; and\n\n(c) be accompanied by any other information or documents\nprescribed by the regulations; and\n\n(d) be accompanied by the fee (if any) prescribed by the\nregulations.\n\n(1AA) However, paragraphs (1)(a) and (b) do not apply to an application\nmade under section 37 (evidence of Australian citizenship) if the\napplication:\n\n(a) is made in a manner prescribed by the regulations; and\n\n(b) contains the information prescribed by the regulations.\n\n(1A) For applications made under section 21 by persons who, in order to\nbe eligible to become an Australian citizen under subsection 21(2),\nmust have sat a test approved in a determination under\nsection 23A, the fee prescribed by the regulations may include a\ncomponent that relates to the sitting of that test.\nApproval of forms\n\n(2) The Minister may, by writing, approve one or more forms for the\npurposes of a provision of this Act under which an application may\nbe made.\nNote:\nFor example, there are 2 ways to become an Australian citizen by\ndescent under section 16. The Minister may approve 1 form for the\npurposes of that section or may approve 2 different forms."
    },
    {
