    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-49",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "49 Evidence of whether computer program is functioning correctly",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-49"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf, p.98",
      "values:originalText": "Issue of notices\n\n(1) In citizenship proceedings, a notice signed by an authorised person\nstating whether or not a specified computer program was\nfunctioning correctly:\n\n(a) at a specified time or during a specified period; and\n\n(b) in relation to specified outcomes from the operation of that\nprogram under an arrangement made under subsection 48(1);\nis prima facie evidence of the matters stated in the notice.\n\n\nOther matters  Part 3\nOther  Division 2\n\nSection 50\n\nAustralian Citizenship Act 2007\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nMinisterial authorisations\n\n(2) The Minister may, by writing, authorise a person to issue notices\nunder this section.\n\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, authorise a class of\npersons to issue notices under this section.\nDefinitions\n\n(4) In this section:\nauthorised person means:\n\n(a) an APS employee in the Department; or\n\n(b) a person authorised under subsection (2) to issue notices\nunder this section; or\n\n(c) any person who is included in a class of persons authorised\nunder subsection (3) to issue notices under this section.\ncitizenship proceedings means:\n\n(a) proceedings in a court (including criminal proceedings) that\nrelate to this Act (including an offence against this Act); or\n\n(b) proceedings that relate to an application for review under\nsection 52.\nfunctioning correctly: a computer program is functioning\ncorrectly if:\n\n(a) outcomes from its operation comply with this Act and the\nregulations; and\n\n(b) those outcomes would be valid if they were made by the\nMinister otherwise than by the operation of the computer\nprogram.",
      "skos:definition": "Issue of notices\n\n(1) In citizenship proceedings, a notice signed by an authorised person\nstating whether or not a specified computer program was\nfunctioning correctly:\n\n(a) at a specified time or during a specified period; and\n\n(b) in relation to specified outcomes from the operation of that\nprogram under an arrangement made under subsection 48(1);\nis prima facie evidence of the matters stated in the notice.\n\n\nOther matters  Part 3\nOther  Division 2\n\nSection 50\n\nAustralian Citizenship Act 2007\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nMinisterial authorisations\n\n(2) The Minister may, by writing, authorise a person to issue notices\nunder this section.\n\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, authorise a class of\npersons to issue notices under this section.\nDefinitions\n\n(4) In this section:\nauthorised person means:\n\n(a) an APS employee in the Department; or\n\n(b) a person authorised under subsection (2) to issue notices\nunder this section; or\n\n(c) any person who is included in a class of persons authorised\nunder subsection (3) to issue notices under this section.\ncitizenship proceedings means:\n\n(a) proceedings in a court (including criminal proceedings) that\nrelate to this Act (including an offence against this Act); or\n\n(b) proceedings that relate to an application for review under\nsection 52.\nfunctioning correctly: a computer program is functioning\ncorrectly if:\n\n(a) outcomes from its operation comply with this Act and the\nregulations; and\n\n(b) those outcomes would be valid if they were made by the\nMinister otherwise than by the operation of the computer\nprogram.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-49-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-49-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-49-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-49-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c7f1eda290d378e933dcbf1e0528ac3dcfc9dc368bb7327ca677665bc6499ca4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-49",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "49 Evidence of whether computer program is functioning correctly",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 98,
      "values:originalText": "Issue of notices\n\n(1) In citizenship proceedings, a notice signed by an authorised person\nstating whether or not a specified computer program was\nfunctioning correctly:\n\n(a) at a specified time or during a specified period; and\n\n(b) in relation to specified outcomes from the operation of that\nprogram under an arrangement made under subsection 48(1);\nis prima facie evidence of the matters stated in the notice.\n\n\nOther matters  Part 3\nOther  Division 2\n\nSection 50\n\nAustralian Citizenship Act 2007\n\nCompilation date: 04/06/2026\n\nMinisterial authorisations\n\n(2) The Minister may, by writing, authorise a person to issue notices\nunder this section.\n\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, authorise a class of\npersons to issue notices under this section.\nDefinitions\n\n(4) In this section:\nauthorised person means:\n\n(a) an APS employee in the Department; or\n\n(b) a person authorised under subsection (2) to issue notices\nunder this section; or\n\n(c) any person who is included in a class of persons authorised\nunder subsection (3) to issue notices under this section.\ncitizenship proceedings means:\n\n(a) proceedings in a court (including criminal proceedings) that\nrelate to this Act (including an offence against this Act); or\n\n(b) proceedings that relate to an application for review under\nsection 52.\nfunctioning correctly: a computer program is functioning\ncorrectly if:\n\n(a) outcomes from its operation comply with this Act and the\nregulations; and\n\n(b) those outcomes would be valid if they were made by the\nMinister otherwise than by the operation of the computer\nprogram."
    },
    {
