    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-51b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "51B Reports to Parliament",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-51b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-act-2007.pdf, p.101",
      "values:originalText": "(1) As soon as practicable after a reporting period ends, the Minister\nmust table a report in each House of the Parliament that sets out the\nnumber of applications made under section 36D to which both of\nthe following apply:\n\n(a) the applications were made during the reporting period to\nwhich the report relates or during an earlier reporting period;\n\n(b) the applications relate to persons who, during the reporting\nperiod to which the report relates, were convicted and\nsentenced for one or more serious offences.\n\n(2) The report must not contain information, or content of a document,\nif:\n\n(a) the information or content includes any operationally\nsensitive information (within the meaning of the Independent\nNational Security Legislation Monitor Act 2010); or",
      "skos:definition": "(1) As soon as practicable after a reporting period ends, the Minister\nmust table a report in each House of the Parliament that sets out the\nnumber of applications made under section 36D to which both of\nthe following apply:\n\n(a) the applications were made during the reporting period to\nwhich the report relates or during an earlier reporting period;\n\n(b) the applications relate to persons who, during the reporting\nperiod to which the report relates, were convicted and\nsentenced for one or more serious offences.\n\n(2) The report must not contain information, or content of a document,\nif:\n\n(a) the information or content includes any operationally\nsensitive information (within the meaning of the Independent\nNational Security Legislation Monitor Act 2010); or",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-51b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-act-2007-sec-51b-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "215bc8c0098ae80e35cae9d34ee629c7ae715c388395d7ea2e226cc57cb5b1aa"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-act-2007#sec-51b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "51B Reports to Parliament",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 101,
      "values:originalText": "(1) As soon as practicable after a reporting period ends, the Minister\nmust table a report in each House of the Parliament that sets out the\nnumber of applications made under section 36D to which both of\nthe following apply:\n\n(a) the applications were made during the reporting period to\nwhich the report relates or during an earlier reporting period;\n\n(b) the applications relate to persons who, during the reporting\nperiod to which the report relates, were convicted and\nsentenced for one or more serious offences.\n\n(2) The report must not contain information, or content of a document,\nif:\n\n(a) the information or content includes any operationally\nsensitive information (within the meaning of the Independent\nNational Security Legislation Monitor Act 2010); or"
    },
